---
// /authorities — the passport from the side of market surveillance
// authorities, notified bodies, customs and the Commission.
//
// What each reader may see is read from data/access.json (the battery
// passport's Art. 77(2) access rules, the same file /visibility uses). Checked
// 2026-09-26 against Regulation (EU) 2023/1542 Arts. 77-78, Regulation (EU)
// 2024/1781 Arts. 11 and 13, and the released node: it refuses to issue
// credentials for authority roles, and trusts an authority's credential only
// from an issuer its operator has named.
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";
import Button from "../components/Button.astro";
import access from "../data/access.json";

const title = "For authorities: checking a Digital Product Passport | Odal Node";
const description =
  "What market surveillance authorities, notified bodies and the Commission can read in a battery passport, how access is granted, and how to check a passport's signatures and history without asking the company that issued it.";

const authority = access.audiences.find((a) => a.key === "authority")!;
const points = authority.sees.map((id) => access.points.find((p) => p.id === id)!);

const mailto = `mailto:contact@odal-node.io?subject=${encodeURIComponent("Authority access to passports")}`;
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <Section h1 eyebrow="For authorities" title="Check a passport without taking anyone's word for it." wide>
    <p>
      Every passport served by Odal Node is signed by the company that issued
      it, with an identity on that company's own web domain. You can check the
      signatures and the full history yourself, without Odal and without the
      file leaving your machine.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section eyebrow="What you can read" title="The authority part of a battery passport." tone="muted" wide>
    <p>
      The Batteries Regulation gives notified bodies, market surveillance
      authorities and the Commission these parts of the passport:
    </p>
    <ul class="not-prose m-0 mt-4 grid list-none gap-5 p-0 md:grid-cols-3">
      {points.map((p) => (
        <li class="card m-0 p-5">
          <p class="m-0 text-base font-semibold text-neutral-900">{p.title}</p>
          <p class="m-0 mt-1.5 text-sm leading-body text-neutral-700">{p.note}</p>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-6">
      The Regulation's annex heads point 2 with the Commission alone, but its
      Article 77 gives point 2 to notified bodies and market surveillance
      authorities as well. The test reports are for authorities only. The
      individual battery's own
      history goes to readers with a legitimate interest instead, such as
      recyclers and the battery's buyer. <a href="/visibility">Visibility</a>{" "}
      shows the split field by field. The toy and detergent passports name
      customs authorities too; their details come in later acts.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section eyebrow="How access works" title="A credential from an issuer the company trusts." wide>
    <p>
      The restricted parts open to a reader who presents a credential stating
      their role, signed by an issuer the company running the passport has
      chosen to trust. A company cannot vouch for an authority itself: its
      node refuses to issue credentials for market surveillance, customs or
      notified body roles, because that standing comes from a Member State.
    </p>
    <p>
      There is no EU-wide issuer of authority credentials yet. The ecodesign
      rules let the Commission set out how such credentials are issued and
      checked, and none has been set out so far. Until then, access for an
      authority is arranged with each company, which adds the authority's
      credential issuer to the ones its node trusts.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section eyebrow="Checking a passport" title="What you can confirm on your own." tone="muted" wide>
    <ul class="not-prose m-0 grid list-none gap-5 p-0 md:grid-cols-3">
      <li class="card m-0 p-5">
        <p class="m-0 text-base font-semibold text-neutral-900">That nothing was changed</p>
        <p class="m-0 mt-2 text-sm leading-body text-neutral-700">
          The proof file carries every signature and the whole history. A
          single changed character is caught where it happened.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li class="card m-0 p-5">
        <p class="m-0 text-base font-semibold text-neutral-900">What happened, in order</p>
        <p class="m-0 mt-2 text-sm leading-body text-neutral-700">
          Corrections, suspensions and handovers to another company are part
          of the signed record, not notes kept beside it.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li class="card m-0 p-5">
        <p class="m-0 text-base font-semibold text-neutral-900">Who signed it</p>
        <p class="m-0 mt-2 text-sm leading-body text-neutral-700">
          Compare the identity in the file with the one the company publishes
          on its own web domain. That step ties the keys to the company.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-6">
      <a href="/verify">Verify</a> runs these checks in your browser, and says
      plainly what they do not prove.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section eyebrow="Finding and keeping a passport" title="From the product, and for the long run." wide>
    <p>
      The code on a product leads to its passport's public page. The EU
      registry of passports, which the Commission set up in July 2026, links a
      product's identifier to where its passport is held.
    </p>
    <p>
      A battery passport must stay available even after the company
      responsible for it ceases to exist or leaves the EU market. Odal Node
      exports a passport with its signatures and full history as one signed
      file, which anyone can keep and check later.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section eyebrow="Talk to us" title="Testing authority access." tone="tinted">
    <p>
      If you work for a market surveillance authority, a notified body or the
      Commission and want to test reading a passport served by Odal Node,
      write to us.
    </p>
    <div class="not-prose mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <Button href={mailto}>Email contact@odal-node.io</Button>
      <Button href="/verify" variant="secondary">Verify a proof file</Button>
    </div>
  </Section>
</Base>
